          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has focal epilepsy with focal impaired awareness seizures, beginning at age 25. The epilepsy has a genetic etiology due to a pathogenic DEPDC5 variant, c.4396C>T. The epilepsy is drug responsive.\n\nCurrent Medications:\n- Topiramate\n- Lacosamide\n\nSeizure Burden:\nThe patient is seizure-free, with 0 seizures per month.\n\nAssessment:\nDrug-responsive focal epilepsy with focal impaired awareness seizures, genetically associated with DEPDC5 c.4396C>T.\n\nPlan:\n- Continue topiramate and lacosamide.\n- Continue monitoring seizure burden.\n\nSincerely,\nEpilepsy Clinic",
